## Where things live

- Product docs: docs/product/ (MVP scope is the source of truth for what to build)
- Architecture and decisions: docs/architecture/
- AI layer: src/lib/ai/ (client.ts wrapper, prompts/, guardrails.ts, usage.ts)
- Database: supabase/migrations/
- Evals: evals/

## Rules

- All model calls go through src/lib/ai/client.ts. Do not import provider SDKs elsewhere.
- Prompts live in src/lib/ai/prompts/. When changing one, update its version note and run the evals.
- AI calls run server-side only, require an authenticated user, and go through quota and rate limit checks.
- Every schema change is a migration with RLS policies in the same file. Never create tables from the dashboard.
- The Supabase secret key (src/lib/supabase/admin.ts) is used only in webhooks, cron jobs, and admin tasks.
- New env vars: add to .env.example in the same change and read them through src/lib/env.ts.
- Never print, log, or commit secret values.
- Stay inside docs/product/mvp-scope.md. If a request is outside scope, say so before building it.

## Commands

- `npm run dev`: local dev server
- `npm run build`: production build
- `npm run lint`
- `npm run check:env`: verify env setup (prints no values)
- `npx supabase migration new <name>` then `npx supabase db push`
- `npx tsx evals/run.ts`: run AI evals
